# Jexpress Brand Guide

This is the single source of truth for visual design in this project. Do not introduce colors, fonts, spacing patterns, or UI patterns not defined here.

---

## 1. Typography

### Font Families

| Role | Family | Variable | Tailwind Class |
|---|---|---|---|
| Headings, stats, blockquotes, phone numbers, wordmark | Bebas Neue | `--font-bebas` | `font-heading`, `font-stat`, `font-phone`, `font-wordmark` |
| Body, nav, buttons, eyebrows, forms, labels | Montserrat | `--font-montserrat` | `font-sans`, `font-inter` |

Both fonts are loaded via `next/font/google` in `app/layout.tsx` and applied on `<html>` via CSS variables `--font-bebas` and `--font-montserrat`. Never import fonts manually or use system fallbacks as primary faces.

All `h1`–`h6` and `blockquote` use Bebas Neue via base styles (`var(--font-bebas), 'Bebas Neue', sans-serif`). Use `font-heading`, `font-stat`, `font-phone`, or `font-wordmark` utilities on non-heading display text. Body copy inherits Montserrat from `font-sans` on `<body>`.

### Font Weights

| Weight | Usage |
|---|---|
| Bebas Neue (400 via `font-heading`) | All headings, stats, blockquotes, large phone numbers, wordmark |
| `font-bold` (700) | CTA button labels (Montserrat) |
| `font-semibold` (600) | Badge labels, eyebrow kickers, tag labels |
| `font-medium` (500) | Nav links, sub-labels |
| `font-normal` (400) | Body paragraphs, descriptions |

### Type Scale & Responsive Sizing

| Element | Mobile | Tablet (`sm`) | Desktop (`lg`) | Extra Large (`xl`) |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `<h1>` hero | `text-4xl` | `text-5xl` | `text-6xl` | `text-7xl` |
| `<h1>` inner page | `text-4xl` | `text-5xl` | `text-6xl` | — |
| `<h2>` section | `text-3xl` | `text-4xl` | `text-5xl` | — |
| `<h3>` card/item | `text-xl` | `text-2xl` | — | — |
| Body / description | `text-base` | `text-lg` | — | — |
| Small body | `text-sm` | — | — | — |
| UI meta / labels | `text-xs` | — | — | — |

Bebas Neue reads smaller than Montserrat at the same pixel size. Default `h3` styles in `globals.css` use `text-xl sm:text-2xl` so headings stay visibly larger than `text-sm` body copy. Do not set card `h3` to `text-lg` or `text-base` when body is `text-sm`.

### Line Heights & Tracking

- Headings: `leading-tight`
- Body paragraphs: `leading-relaxed`
- Section eyebrow labels: `tracking-[0.2em]` (handled automatically by `.eyebrow-dash`)
- Nav links: `tracking-wide`
- Footer headings / key area labels: `tracking-widest`
- Use `text-balance` on all multi-line headings to prevent orphans.

### Eyebrow Labels (Section Labels)

All section eyebrow labels **must** use the `.eyebrow-dash` CSS utility class. Never use an inline `border-l-4` span pattern.

```tsx
{/* On light backgrounds */}
<span className="eyebrow-dash text-[#d4a53a] mb-4">Section Name</span>

{/* On dark (brand-blue) backgrounds */}
<span className="eyebrow-dash text-[#d4a53a] mb-4">Section Name</span>

{/* In hero sections on dark bg (slightly muted) */}
<span className="eyebrow-dash text-white/70 mb-4">Section Name</span>
```

The `.eyebrow-dash` class (defined in `app/globals.css`) provides: `inline-flex`, `items-center`, `gap-0.65rem`, Montserrat font, `text-xs`, `font-semibold`, `uppercase`, `letter-spacing: 0.2em`, and a gold `::before` dash pseudo-element. Do **not** duplicate these properties inline.

