## 3. Buttons

### Primary Button (CTA) — Gold

```tsx
className="inline-flex items-center gap-2 bg-[#d4a53a] hover:bg-[#d4a53a] text-white font-bold text-base px-8 py-4 rounded-full transition-all duration-200 hover:scale-105 active:scale-95 shadow-xl shadow-[#d4a53a]/40"
```

- Shape: `rounded-full`
- Default padding: `px-8 py-4` (large), `px-6 py-2.5` (compact header)
- Font: `font-bold`, `text-base` (large) or `text-sm` (compact)
- Hover: scale up `hover:scale-105`
- Active: scale down `active:scale-95`
- Shadow: `shadow-xl shadow-[#d4a53a]/40` (large), `shadow-lg shadow-[#d4a53a]/30` (compact)

### Secondary Button — Brand Blue (solid)

```tsx
className="inline-flex items-center gap-2 bg-brand-blue hover:bg-brand-blue text-white font-bold text-base px-8 py-4 rounded-full transition-all duration-200 hover:scale-105 active:scale-95 shadow-xl shadow-[#00193c]/40"
```

- Same shape, padding, and motion as primary
- Use when a secondary action exists alongside a gold primary CTA
- Do **not** use the old ghost/outline `border-2 border-white/30` pattern for marketing CTAs

### Ghost / Outline Button

```tsx
className="inline-flex items-center gap-2 border-2 border-white/30 hover:border-[#d4a53a] text-white hover:text-[#d4a53a] font-semibold text-base px-8 py-4 rounded-full transition-all duration-200"
```

- Reserved for nav-level compact actions only (e.g. header "Book Now" outline variant)
- Not used in marketing section CTAs

### Rules

- All buttons use `transition-all duration-200`
- All marketing CTA buttons include `<RiArrowRightLine size={18} />` icon
- Disabled state: `opacity-50 pointer-events-none`
- Never use square corners (`rounded-md`) on marketing CTA buttons — always `rounded-full`

